# Command: Test Suite Execution

## Purpose

Run automated tests for the NestJS API.

## API unit tests

From `api/`:

```bash
npm run test          # all unit tests (CI parity)
npm run test:cov      # with coverage
npm run test:watch    # watch mode
```

## E2E (local only)

```bash
npm run test:e2e
```

Requires a valid `DATABASE_URL` and a real test module. Not in CI yet.

## CI

`.github/workflows/api-ci.yml` on `api/**` push/PR:

```text
db:generate → lint → build → test
```

No database connection required for the CI test job.

## Frontend

No automated test suite configured. Use `cd web && npm run lint && npm run build` for quality checks.

## Constraints

- Mock Prisma in unit tests; never hit production Neon.
- Co-locate `*.spec.ts` with the file under test.

Coverage priorities: `.cursor/rules/test.mdc`.
